WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.337
The authorizing official sits outside
the program and above the record.

2
00:00:04.337 --> 00:00:07.888
The role is small in time
and large in consequence.

3
00:00:07.888 --> 00:00:09.908
The program asks four things of it:

4
00:00:09.908 --> 00:00:12.793
sign for every gap it
carries rather than closes;

5
00:00:12.793 --> 00:00:17.771
keep reviewing whether the risk is still
acceptable; decide whether a significant

6
00:00:17.771 --> 00:00:22.388
change needs reauthorization; and set
how independent the assessors must be.

7
00:00:22.388 --> 00:00:27.370
Their representative can do the daily work,
but risk acceptance can't be delegated,

8
00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:30.374
and a contractor can prepare
one but never sign it.

9
00:00:30.374 --> 00:00:34.662
The decision for the authorizing
official: receive a monthly posture

10
00:00:34.662 --> 00:00:38.875
report built from the record, and
sign every open-ended gap in writing.

11
00:00:38.875 --> 00:00:41.420
Next, the record as a federal record.
